            "review_title": "Review at Vị Noodles - Ramen & Matcha Latte",
            "review_text": "Hannah Tr\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam2 contributions\n0\nVị Noodles - Stumbled Upon a New Hidden Ramen Gem in District 7!\nMar 2025 • Business\nIf you're a ramen lover on the hunt for a spot that’s delicious – affordable – authentic, then this cozy little shop next to the medical area in Phú Mỹ Hưng is a must-visit!\n\n📍 Don’t let the humble space fool you—this place can easily rival the quality of famous ramen spots in the Little Japan area of District 1.\n\n🍜 The fresh noodles have an appealing golden color. I like mine on the chewier side, so I asked the chef to make them a bit firmer—perfect!\n\n🍥 Toppings were spot on: the marinated soft-boiled egg was perfectly jammy (just the way I like it), and the chashu was tender, sliced thicker than most ramen places I’ve tried.\n\n🍜 The broth here is house-made, simmered from pork bones and meat for around 18 hours, according to the owner. When I visited, they were in the middle of prepping the soup—it smelled amazing. The staff was super friendly and happy to help recommend the best ramen to suit your taste. Bonus: they speak English, Russian, and Japanese!\n\nNot only is the quality top-notch, but the price is incredibly reasonable—cheaper than many ramen spots in District 1. I had a special Hakata bowl with 150gr for just around 152,000 VND.\n\n🥤 The Matcha Latte + Shiratama was a delightful surprise. Normally, I’d have to trek to D1 to find this kind of drink, but here it’s a must-try. Rich matcha, not too sweet, well-balanced with just the right amount of milk, and the shiratama had that perfect chewy texture.\n\nAbsolutely loved it—I’ll definitely be back to try their mazesoba and chashudon in my next business trip!\nRead more\nWritten April 8, 2025",
